          "reasoning": "**Considering constraints on titles**\n\nI need to include specific constraints for titles. First, I won't allow titles shorter than three characters or trimming issues, likely just whitespace. If someone submits a title that's too long, like over 80 characters, the response should be 422. Importantly, if the title is omitted during the update, I should allow a description patch without revalidating the original title. Existing titles longer than 80 characters should still remain retrievable. Keeping track of these rules is essential!**Clarifying title updates**\n\nWhen a title is provided as null, the instructions indicate that I shouldn't revalidate the original title. I should consider the differences between PUT and PATCH semantics. For PATCH, if the title is omitted during an update, then title validation should be skipped. However, for PUT, a full replacement is needed, and the title must be validated. This also applies when just updating the description. It seems like there's a clear pathway for how to handle these updates.**Defining update semantics**\n\nTypically, PUT requires a full replacement, including a title; if it's omitted, the server might set a default. However, I think it's clearer to instruct that PATCH treats omitted titles as partial updates and skips validation. For PUT, the title should be required and validated. I need to define this behavior and document it thoroughly. Also, the asset version must increase on successful updates, even if the existing title is over 80 characters. I’ll consider necessary code changes and database constraints while ensuring existing titles remain valid.**Ensuring database constraints**\n\nIf the database has an 80-character limit, it could create issues. I think it's important to ensure the database column can accommodate existing longest titles, so it should remain at least 120 characters. I suggest we check the schema and avoid reducing the column length. For implementation, I'll update validation constants, incorporating trimming and setting the minimum length to 3 and a maximum of 80 when the title is present. I'll preserve existing titles and create necessary tests to ensure everything works as expected!",
